\title{Equivalence classes}
\date{2026-03-04T03:00:19Z}
\tag{discrete}
\tag{draft}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{So, what kinds of things can we say about [equivalence relations](008Z) in general? First, let’s define the important concept of an \em{equivalence class}.}

\transclude{0097}
\transclude{0099}
\transclude{009A}

\p{Suppose we have two elements #{a, b \in A}. What can we say about the potential relationship between their equivalence classes, #{[a]} and #{[b]}? It turns out there are only two possibilities: either they are exactly the same, or they do not overlap at all.}

\transclude{009B}


